# LinkedIn Search Scraper

Chrome extension that scrapes LinkedIn people-search results from a filter URL and exports JSON. Full orientation: [AGENTS.md](mdc:AGENTS.md).

## Priorities

- Prefer official / user-authorized data paths over scraping.
- Incremental sync + cache; never hammer LinkedIn.
- Keep auth material and dumped data out of the repo and out of chat logs.

## Do not

- Commit or echo cookies, `li_at`, OAuth tokens, or `.env` values.
- Check in large `data/` / dump files.
- Add frameworks or abstractions before the first working fetch path exists.

## Stack (bootstrapped)

Chrome MV3 + TypeScript/React (Vite/CRXJS). See [AGENTS.md](mdc:AGENTS.md) and [linkedin-crawl.mdc](mdc:linkedin-crawl.mdc).

## When changing stack

Update [AGENTS.md](mdc:AGENTS.md) stack table and add focused rules (one concern per `.mdc`) instead of bloating this file.
